{"id": "20260702013903842487_3bd1e3b3", "type": "Evidence", "text": "One question asks why Prescott is so unwavering in 
building a boys’ boarding school. The answer explains that Prescott was educated at a boys’ boarding school founded by 
Horace, a religious fanatic who instilled discipline and inspired his students. Prescott became close to Horace and 
promised to follow in his footsteps by establishing his own boys’ boarding school.", "source_ids": 
["20260702013901064858_0f0aef2c"], "citations": [2], "sources": [{"source_id": "20260702013901064858_0f0aef2c", "title":
