null}]}, {"id": "20260702013903933708_37b68431", "type": "Evidence", "text": "Cordelia is depicted as rebellious and 
bold, frequently challenging her father when she disagrees. She is angered by his decision to focus on a boys’ school 
rather than programs to empower his daughters and other girls, viewing this as favoritism toward men. The commentary 
notes that Cordelia even speculates her father might be gay because his emotional focus seems to be on men and boys 
rather than women.", "source_ids": ["20260702013901064858_0f0aef2c"], "citations": [2], "sources": [{"source_id": 
