null}]}, {"id": "20260702013904030942_08c259fa", "type": "Evidence", "text": "A third question discusses why the school 
board forces Prescott to retire as headmaster. The answer stresses Prescott’s strong attachment to the Episcopal school 
he built with his own resources and has led since its founding. However, at age 82, his efficiency has declined, in 
movement and thinking, raising concerns among the board. The board, having authority to remove the head, compels his 
retirement so that a younger, more energetic man named David (described as taking over the position) can lead the 
school.", "source_ids": ["20260702013901064858_0f0aef2c"], "citations": [2], "sources": [{"source_id": 
